figdown 0.1 topology
# `RULE-POSITION-ENUMERATION`: `plane=` is an ID-VALUED option, and `badOpts` has
# applied the id rule to `in=`/`plane=` (`QUOTED-IDS`). `edge` does
# not go through `badOpts`, so it was the ONE id position in the language
# that tolerated a quoted id: `node c "C" plane="over"` was a line error and
# `edge a -> b plane="over"` was accepted. One missing call.
plane over "Overlay" z-index=2
node a "A"
node b "B"
node c "C" plane="over"
edge a -> b plane="over"
